---
/**
 * 官网隐私政策（与当前产品实现对齐；非律师意见书）。
 * 生效日与正文重大变更时同步改产品文档与 Settings 摘要外链。
 */
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro'
import '../styles/pages.css'

const effectiveDate = '2026-10-26'
const contactEmail = 'privacy@yiveno.com'
---

<MainLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · Yiveno"
  description="How Yiveno handles personal data for the Chrome extension and website: local-first memory, optional cloud sync, account, and AI."
>
  <article class="page">
    <header>
      <h1 class="page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page__meta">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <section class="page__prose" lang="en">
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how <strong>Yiveno</strong> (“we”, “us”) handles information
        when you use the Yiveno Chrome extension, the website at yiveno.com, and related backend
        services (Cloudflare Workers). Yiveno helps you <strong>find what you saved</strong>:
        Capture with low friction, then Recall into a short list of closest fits — you choose. It is
        not a bookmark manager, note-taking app, chat bot, or “AI organizer” as a primary promise.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today Yiveno is operated by an <strong>individual</strong> based in{' '}
        <strong>Hangzhou, China</strong> (not yet a registered company). We may later transfer
        operations to a company registered in Hangzhou; if that happens, we will update this Policy
        and the effective date. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The browser extension (Chromium — Microsoft Edge and Google Chrome) is{' '}
        <strong>not yet listed</strong> for public install on the <strong>Chrome Web Store</strong>{' '}
        or <strong>Microsoft Edge Add-ons</strong>, and we are <strong>not yet charging</strong> the
        public for paid plans. Product pages may describe planned Free / Pro features; they are not
        a claim of a live paid customer base. When listed, mainland desktop install prefers Edge
        Add-ons (see product docs · ADR-020).
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <h3>2.1 On your device (default)</h3>
      <p>
        By default, memories you Capture (for example text excerpts, related page metadata you
        choose to save, and your notes) are stored in the extension’s local IndexedDB on your
        browser profile. Uninstalling the extension typically removes this local store.
      </p>
      <h3>2.2 Account (optional sign-in)</h3>
      <p>
        If you sign in via the website — email one-time code (or magic link), or Google / Microsoft
        OAuth through our auth provider — we process account identifiers such as user id, email, and
        profile fields the provider shares (for example display name or avatar URL).{' '}
        <strong>Signing in does not by itself upload your memories.</strong>
      </p>
      <h3>2.3 Cloud memory (opt-in sync)</h3>
      <p>
        Only after you explicitly enable cloud sync in the extension do we store{' '}
        <strong>text excerpts</strong> (and sync backups) in our cloud database (currently
        Supabase), scoped to your account. The Supabase primary database for production is in{' '}
        <strong>East US (Ohio)</strong>, AWS region <strong>us-east-2</strong>.{' '}
        <strong>Bookmark entries imported from Chrome stay on this device</strong>
        and are not merged across devices through Yiveno cloud sync. Turning sync off does{' '}
        <strong>not</strong>
        automatically delete cloud copies; you can delete cloud memories or delete your account from
        Settings → Data.
      </p>
      <h3>2.4 AI / language features</h3>
      <p>
        Some features (for example understanding what you typed) may send limited requests through
        our servers to a model provider. The model does not directly create, change, or delete what
        you saved. We do not default to sending your entire library to a model.
      </p>
      <h3>2.5 Waitlist (optional)</h3>
      <p>
        If you leave an email on yiveno.com to be notified when the extension is ready to install,
        we store that email so we can send that notice. We do not add waitlist addresses to a
        marketing list.
      </p>
      <h3>2.6 Extension uninstall feedback (optional)</h3>
      <p>
        When you remove the Chrome extension, Chrome may open a short page on yiveno.com (best
        effort; not gated on website or extension sign-in). You may optionally pick closed-set
        reasons and leave a short note. If a one-time uninstall token is present (you were signed in
        to the extension), the page also clears the <strong>extension</strong> remote session — not
        your website login, and not your local or cloud Memory. Feedback is optional and not tied to
        reinstalling. We store the reasons, note, and technical context needed to improve the
        product and reproduce issues (for example approximate IP, browser user-agent, language,
        timezone, screen size, and — if you are signed in on the website — display name and account
        email). Retention is short; we may email a copy to our internal feedback inbox. We do not
        use this form to delete your library or sign you out of the website. Bugs or account issues
        that need a reply should go to
        <a href="mailto:support@yiveno.com">support@yiveno.com</a>, not the optional uninstall form.
      </p>
      <h3>2.7 What we do not collect by default</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Your full browsing History</li>
        <li>Always-on clipboard reading</li>
        <li>Full webpage content you did not actively Capture</li>
        <li>Uploading memories to the cloud without enabling sync</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>2.8 Usage signals on your library</h3>
      <p>
        To improve Recall ordering on <strong>your</strong> device, Yiveno may store how you
        interact with saved items — for example how often you open a result, or when you dismiss
        “none of these.” These signals describe your relationship with <strong>your</strong>{' '}
        library; they are not sold as a separate product asset.
      </p>
      <h3>2.9 Per-item derived recall helpers</h3>
      <p>
        Yiveno may compute recall helpers bound to a specific saved item — for example tags or
        keywords inferred from its title or excerpt, or math helpers stored with the item so fuzzy
        finding works better. These stay with the item in your local library (and in your cloud copy
        if sync is on). They help retrieve <strong>your</strong> content; we do not treat them as
        Yiveno-owned secrets you cannot export.
      </p>

      <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide Capture and Recall on your device</li>
        <li>Authenticate you and optional cloud sync when you enable it</li>
        <li>
          Operate, secure, and debug the service (including Worker logs with limited previews where
          needed)
        </li>
        <li>
          Process subscriptions or payments if you purchase paid plans (billing records may be
          retained as required by law)
        </li>
        <li>Email you if you joined the install waitlist, when a spot is available</li>
        <li>
          Review optional uninstall feedback (closed-set reason and short note) if you choose to
          send it
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Processors and subprocessors</h2>
      <p>Depending on features you use, data may be processed by:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supabase</strong> — authentication, (when sync is on) cloud Memory storage, and
          waitlist emails if you join; production primary database region <strong>us-east-2</strong>{' '}
          (East US / Ohio)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — Workers API, hosting, KV for optional uninstall feedback,
          Email Sending when enabled, Turnstile bot checks on email sign-in, and related
          infrastructure
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email delivery (via our auth provider’s mail path / configured SMTP)</strong> — if
          you sign in with an email code or magic link
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google / Microsoft</strong> — if you choose their OAuth sign-in
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Model providers</strong> — only when an AI feature you use is routed through our
          Worker
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payment providers</strong> (Dodo Payments) — if you purchase a subscription
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Retention and deletion</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Local memories</strong> remain until you delete them, clear leftover account data,
          or remove the extension.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloud memories</strong> remain while your account exists and sync data has not
          been deleted; you can delete all cloud memories without deleting the account.
        </li>
        <li>
          To manage storage redundancy, we may periodically prune certain cloud-related data, such
          as sync backups and soft-deleted billing records. For example, sync backups keep only the
          most recent snapshots (currently up to 5 per account), and soft-deleted
          subscription/payment history is removed after 180 days.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Waitlist emails</strong> are kept until we have notified you, you ask us to remove
          the address, or we no longer need the list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Uninstall feedback</strong> (reason and optional note) is kept in short-lived
          storage for product improvement, and may also appear in our feedback email inbox. It is
          not tied to your account login.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Delete account</strong> (Settings → Data) removes cloud Memory and backups, closes
          the auth user, clears this account’s local Memory bucket on that device, and signs you
          out. Billing records may be retained in anonymized or legally required form and are not a
          recoverable login.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Data ownership and export</h2>
      <p>
        Yiveno is local-first: you should be able to <strong>take, clear, and leave</strong> with
        your library. Export is a product responsibility, not a paid perk.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Your content</strong> — excerpts, notes, URLs, and bookmark traces you chose to
          save — belongs to you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your in-library usage</strong> — open/dismiss signals and timestamps on your items
          — belongs to you as part of your library history.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Per-item recall helpers</strong> — inferred tags/keywords and matching helpers
          stored on an item — stay with that item in your backup; they are not withheld as separate
          Yiveno property.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Yiveno service layer</strong> — de-identified aggregate statistics or
          non-individualized models used to improve the product for everyone — is not included in
          your personal export and is cut off from you when you delete your account, to the extent
          we store individual links.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Full backup export</strong> (Settings → Data) downloads your current identity’s
        local Memory as JSON, including soft-deleted items and the fields above. A lighter
        “portable” export for moving to other tools may be added later; it would not replace full
        backup.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use Yiveno without signing in (local profile)</li>
        <li>Sign in without enabling cloud sync</li>
        <li>Enable or disable cloud sync</li>
        <li>
          Export a full backup, delete cloud memories, or delete your account from Settings → Data
        </li>
        <li>Review a short privacy notice in Settings → Privacy before enabling sync</li>
        <li>Send optional uninstall feedback after removing the extension</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Yiveno is not directed to children under 13 (or the minimum age required in your
        jurisdiction). Do not use the service if you are under that age.
      </p>

      <h2>9. International users</h2>
      <p>
        The operator is based in Hangzhou, China. Account data and (when sync is on) cloud Memory
        are stored with Supabase in the <strong>United States</strong> (primary database:{' '}
        <strong>East US / Ohio, us-east-2</strong>). Other processors (for example Cloudflare
        Workers, AI model providers, and payment providers if you purchase a plan) may process data
        in the United States and other locations where they operate. If you enable cloud sync or
        sign in, you understand your account and synced data may be stored outside your country of
        residence.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Policy as the product changes. We will update the effective date on this
        page. Material changes to the in-extension sync notice may require you to re-confirm before
        turning sync on again.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. Product help and
        complaints:
        <a href="/support">Support</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="page__note">
        This page reflects how Yiveno works today. It is not legal advice. Features not marked
        available in the product are not claimed here as shipped.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
